          "4.12 Lists LLEEAARRNNIINNGG OOUUTTCCOOMMEESS 2.3.9 Use list values with appropriate operators, built-in functions and methods (limited to those mentioned in the Quick Reference Guide) to perform:",
          "• Concatenation and repetition • Extraction of single items and subset of items (i.e., indexing and slicing) • Testing of whether an item is in the list • Calculation of length • Calculation of sum, minimum value and maximum value (provided the list items are all integer or floating-point values) A list is an ordered sequence of changeable values.",
