          "6.4.1 Using Print Statements One simple yet effective debugging technique is to keep track of how variables change as the program runs using the print() function. By adding a print statement that outputs the value of important variables inside a loop, we can get valuable information on how the variables change over time. For instance, the program below has been modified with the addition of line 9, which prints out the values of index and acronym each time the loop repeats.",
