          "parity bit to detect errors Original data bits Parity system - even Data transmission Successful Unsuccessful 1010001 11010001 11010001 11110001 Total number of Total number of 1-bits is even 1-bits is odd Table 10.7 Successful and failed data transmission in an even parity system If the same packet is used in an odd parity system instead, then the parity bit of 0 is added, as there is already an odd number of 1-bits in the original data string.",
