          "If the data transmission is successful, the total number of 1-bits detected would be odd, which is the same as that at the source. This means that the data is error-free. However, if there is a simple error in the data transmission, the total number of 1-bits detected would be even, which differs from that at the source. This means that the data is corrupted.",
          "Parity checking has certain limitations. For instance, it can detect that an error has occurred but cannot determine where the error occurred.",
