          "Figure 10.38 Viewing a web page hosted on a device in a separate network Note that in this example, we have manually configured the IP addresses, subnet masks and gateways for each computer. However, for most home networks, this is usually not needed as computers are automatically configured using the Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol (DHCP). As a challenge, try setting up the simulated network to use DHCP. To learn more, right-click any of the devices and select “Show data exchange” to explore the individual packets that are sent and received as part of the simulation.",
