          "In general, cookies are not malicious and are needed to keep track of authentication information to identify which users are currently logged in. However, they can also be used to keep track of user movements and preferences within the website, such as which pages were most recently visited by the user or how the user wants the site to be presented. Even worse, advertising companies with advertisements on multiple websites can also use cookies to keep track of users as they move from one website to another. In this way, cookies can be a threat to data privacy.",
