          "Table 14.1 Common tasks that can be performed by AI DID YOU KKNNOOWW??",
          "As of 2024, most AI systems are still considered “narrow AI” or “weak AI” that are designed to excel only in specific tasks such as the ones in Table 14.1. This contrasts with the concept of an Artificial General Intelligence (AGI) or “strong AI” that can apply its intelligence to solve any problem with the same competence as a human being.",
          "However, some generative AI systems show early signs of being able to solve problems across a wide range of domains, either at or beyond human-level performance. Many of these systems are Large Language Models (LLMs) that have been trained on a massive amount of text. Despite their impressive capabilities, these systems are still not considered AGI due to limitations such as their tendency to make up fictitious details (see section 14.1.5.5) or to make choices or mistakes that humans would not make, especially in tasks unrelated to language processing. Nevertheless, the steady advancement of LLMs represents significant progress towards the goal of eventually producing an AGI.",
          "14.1.3 Machine Learning Machine Learning (ML) is an important technique used in AI that enables a computer to perform complex tasks without explicit programming.",
