          "Table 14.3 Key terminology in Machine Learning 14.1.4.2 Algorithm The NN method operates on the principle that similar data points with the same label have similar features and thus would be closer together when plotted on a graph using the features as coordinates. For this textbook, we will limit ourselves to two quantitative features so data points can always be plotted on a 2D graph.",
