          "Underfitting (machine learning) Instead of only looking at just one nearest neighbour, When an ML model is too simple to learn the k-nearest neighbours algorithm looks at the k the underlying patterns of the training nearest neighbours and outputs the most common data label out of the k neighbours. This makes the algorithm more robust and less sensitive to outliers or noisy training data.",
